---
const strengths = [
  {
    title: 'Technology without building it',
    body: 'I know how systems are architected, where technology enables and where it limits, and how to make smart product decisions without writing a line of code — sitting with engineers, designers, and users in the same conversation and translating between all three.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Communication across the whole cycle',
    body: 'I simplify complex ideas for the people who need the big picture, and get granular for the people in the detail — meeting a frontline health worker in Jharkhand and a country director in a boardroom with exactly what each needs to do their best work.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Fast learning, real network',
    body: 'I work at the edge of what I know — shipping blockchain products in six months, understanding packaging software architecture, designing health interventions across nine states — by reaching out, asking, learning, and bringing it back into the work.',
  },
];
---

<section id="philosophy" class="relative bg-ink px-6 py-28 sm:px-10 sm:py-36">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
    <p data-reveal class="font-sans text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-signal">
      Philosophy
    </p>

    <h2
      data-reveal
      data-reveal-delay="0.08"
      class="text-balance mt-6 max-w-3xl font-display text-3xl font-medium leading-tight text-paper sm:text-5xl"
    >
      The most important question lives before the brief is written — not <span class="text-accent">what</span> to build, but <span class="text-accent">why</span> it needs to exist at all.
    </h2>

    <p
      data-reveal
      data-reveal-delay="0.16"
      class="mt-8 max-w-2xl font-sans text-lg leading-relaxed text-paper-dim"
    >
      That's the stage I'm drawn to — reading user behaviour, designing experiments, iterating on
      what the data says, and making hard calls about what to build and what to let go. Then
      pitching it, getting engineering and leadership on board, and seeing it through to shipped.
    </p>

    <div data-reveal-group class="mt-20 grid gap-10 sm:grid-cols-3 sm:gap-8">
      {
        strengths.map((strength) => (
          <div data-reveal-item class="border-t border-paper-dim/20 pt-6">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-paper">{strength.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper-dim">{strength.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
